# NO LINE-ENDING CONVERSION, AND THIS PACKAGE SHIPS BINARIES.
#
# `Frameworks/RecklessFFI.xcframework` tracks `libcreckless.a` for every Apple
# slice directly in git, alongside its headers. Git's binary heuristic usually
# spares an archive, because it looks for a NUL byte in the first 8000; that is
# a heuristic, and the difference between a real engine archive and a corrupt
# one is the difference this package exists to keep honest.
#
# MEASURED on FianchettoKit's Windows CI, 2026-09-01 (run 33480101316), before
# any of these files existed. GitHub's windows-latest runners set
# `core.autocrlf=true` globally, so `actions/checkout` rewrote every LF to CRLF
# and eleven of fourteen test failures were that one cause. Each corrupted
# fixture had grown by exactly its own newline count, and one of them was a
# BINARY ML fixture that gained a byte and lost its SHA-256.
#
# `.gitattributes` overrides `core.autocrlf`, travels with the repository, and
# applies to every consumer — so a developer cloning on Windows gets the same
# bytes CI does. Configuring CI alone would have fixed CI alone.
#
# `* -text` rather than a per-extension list on purpose: the default has to be
# "do not touch", because the next byte-sensitive file will be added by someone
# who has never read this file.
* -text
